::node[notion_brain_dump]
->[:role=skill]
->[:keywords=brain dump, notes, tasks, ideas, organize, notion]

::dense
Transforms raw, chaotic user thoughts into perfectly structured Notion database entries.
Assumes the presence of the native `notion_database_create_page` tool.

::steps
1. Ingest the user's unstructured text input.
2. Use your internal intelligence to segment the input into distinct items (e.g., separating grocery items from project ideas or urgent tasks).
3. For each identified item, determine the most logical Notion database it belongs to (e.g., "Tasks", "Journal", "Ideas", "Reading List").
4. If the user hasn't specified which databases to use, politely ask for the database IDs or names before proceeding.
5. Loop through the items and call the `notion_database_create_page` tool for each one, structuring the properties (Tags, Status, Title) appropriately.
6. Provide a concise summary to the user confirming exactly what was saved and where.

::assertions
assert user_input != "" "The user must provide some thoughts or text to organize."
